From 574f0c839b6d0c67cf91ebf199522ca456856bdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirk Brown <kdborg@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 16:37:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Mersey: console dropdown, Sources debugging bridge, drawer
 panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Console: JavaScript/Mersey language selector (persisted setting) in the
  toolbar; Mersey turns go to the fork's Mersey CDP domain, never the JS
  evaluator; completions in Mersey mode come from Mersey.completions via a
  CodeMirror `override`, so no JS global can appear.
- Sources bridge (panels/mersey/mersey-meta.ts, late-initialization
  runnable — meta modules evaluate before MainImpl boots and boot replaces
  app singletons): serves executed Mersey scripts as Sources files (real
  URL for external .mersey modules, "<page>.mersey" for inline blocks),
  translates gutter breakpoints to engine lines (sole writer — REPLACE
  semantics tolerate no second writer), reveals the paused line, and
  routes the STANDARD toggle-pause/step actions to the Mersey engine while
  it is paused. window.__merseyDebug is the in-page ground-truth handle.
- Drawer panel: stack/scopes/stepping, auto-opened on pause (a pause that
  presents nothing reads as a hung page); consumes a pause that fired
  before the panel opened.
- Generated protocol refreshed from the fork's Mersey.pdl (concatenated
  with v8's js_protocol.pdl — omitting it silently drops Runtime/Debugger).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
